gossipcop-908591,https://www.tvguide.com/news/how-to-get-away-with-murder-season-5-spoilers/,How to Get Away with Murder Season 5 Spoilers: Everything We Know,956218297871200257	956220081180233728	956220111345668096	956220578234601472	956221592299696128	956222539264675842	956224709124935680	956224796823613440	956225761618227200	956229822489026561	956249474107617281	956269413594025985	957445151898484737,0,tvguide.com,65,"How to Get Away with Murder 's Season 4 finale gave us more answers than questions for once, but that doesn't mean we're not still ready and eager for more Murder Club mysteries.
After winning her Supreme Court Case, Annalise ( Viola Davis ) returned home to win Laurel's ( Karla Souza ) baby back and get her debauched daddy arrested by the FBI. Frankly, there were enough loose ends wrapped up to make the Season 4 finale a series finale, but thankfully ABC disagreed and renewed the show for another year.
You know what that means... It's time to gather up everything we know about Season 5 to start figuring out how all these puzzle pieces will come together when How to Get Away with Murder returns!
Gabriel Maddox is a major player. Rome Flynn has officially been upped to series regular for Season 5, meaning whoever this kid is, he's important. So far, all we know is that Frank ( Charlie Weber ) recognizes him on sight and apparently knows his mother. But who else was on the end of that call?
How to Get Away with Murder Finale: Who Is Gabriel Maddox?
Bonnie's ( Liza Weil ) kid could be alive. Thanks to Denver's ( Benito Martinez ) files, we now know Bonnie's baby (who she thought died in childbirth) might be alive and kicking and walking around out there somewhere. There was a DNA match between Bonnie and an unknown third party in those files with ""kid alive?"" marked in the margins, so the good money is on Gabriel Maddox being her long, lost son.
Expect a different kind of flashback/flash-forward. Showrunner Pete Nowalk has said that there will be a different, ""more fun"" tone to the flashback format next season, which might indicate they won't be quite as full of doom and gloom as they've been in the past season.
Nate ( Billy Brown ) holds all the cards. Nate was the one who ended up with all those files Denver was keeping on Annalise and her team, which means the ball is officially in his court. Recently, he's been on Team Annalise, but his loyalties have always shifted when the moral lines turn grey, which means he could cause some serious destruction with all this new knowledge he has.
Viola Davis, How to Get Away with Murder
How to Get Away with Murder : Gabriel Maddox Will Be a Huge Part of Season 5
Laurel might have murdered her mother. The final shot of Laurel in the Season 4 finale revealed that she had some nasty scratches on her arm that were almost definitely made by her mom's nails. She claimed she'd never hurt her own mother, but Sandrine (Lolita Davidovich) went mysteriously missing and has yet to resurface. Paired with the knowledge that Laurel told her to kill herself during their last fight, the evidence is mounting up that Laurel wanted her mom dead.
There's still story left to tell with Marcus (Cornelius Smith Jr.) from Scandal . During the How to Get Away with Murder/ Scandal crossover, Michaela ( Aja Naomi King ) hooked up with Marcus while they were on a stakeout. Even though our hearts were broken for Asher ( Matt McGorry ), there was undeniable chemistry between Michael and Marcus that feels like a major loose end. Smith hasn't officially joined the cast, but showrunner Pete Nowalk has hinted that it's a possibility and Michael and Marcus' story isn't over yet.
A Coliver wedding is still on the books. It feels like we've been waiting forever for this wedding, which is why we were relieved to hear that chances are good we'll finally see Connor ( Jack Falahee ) and Oliver ( Conrad Ricamora ) exchange vows next season. Don't expect it to be a run of the mill wedding though. Nowalk warns. ""I will say, I personally kind of hate weddings, and I hate the trope of it, so we're going to do it in our own fun way.""
Michaela is on a dark path. Now that she's turned Simon over to be deported and cheated her way out of her relationship with Asher, Michaela is headed down a darker path than we've ever seen her on before. She's becoming more and more like Annalise, which could be a great or terrible thing for her depending on how you look at it.
How to Get Away with Murder 's first three seasons are available to stream on Netflix now.",ok
gossipcop-879571,https://www.foxnews.com/entertainment/dwts-recap-property-brothers-drew-scott-and-dancing-partner-emma-slater-reveal-wedding-plans,'DWTS' recap: 'Property Brothers'' Drew Scott and dancing partner Emma Slater reveal wedding plans,907799600177860613	907801247377510400	907801271939289089	907801786764972032	907802821336039424	907802830232330240	907802903871664128	907803364100112385	907803412317708288	907803457347899392	907806057019215873	907809962826588160	907812895643328512	907824277633814529	907825216419753985	907840192161206273	907851182701506560	907851198635671553	907851307310075904	907851374083411968	907851397714018310	907851450289664001	907851505281245184	907851504836640768	907851612617670656	907851627775885312	907851644158844931	907851649250742272	907851702417727488	907851723733168128	907851764510199812	907851905929539585	907851939756564480	907851975898918913	907852132572913665	907852152097439745	907852158653095937	907852163027755008	907852182136946688	907852179037462528	907852190538244096	907852241087975424	907852486760976385	907862707466108928	907865310543446021	907867653011800064	907874026126680064	907874426695254016	907937155628093440	907973936188715009,0,foxnews.com,98,"Fox411: Actress Sasha Pieterse and 'Property Brothers' star Drew Scott reveal they have lost 37 and 30 pounds respectively thanks to training for the competition series.
Drew Scott and his ""Dancing with the Stars"" partner Emma Slater have been juggling more than just the competition as both stars plan their weddings!
While the ""Property Brothers"" star is marrying his fiancée Linda Phan next year, Slater got engaged last fall – live on ""DWTS"" -- to fellow pro dancer Sasha Farber and is finalizing details of their nuptials.
On Monday night, after Scott and Slater learned they were advancing to the ""DWTS"" finals, they filled reporters in on their personal joy. Both are twins and couldn't be happier to be getting married to their longtime loves.
Drew Scott wore a kilt for his Monday night tango and told Fox News after the show that it's a good warm up for his wedding to Phan, in which he also plans to honor his Scottish heritage.
""I'm going to wear a kilt to my wedding,"" Scott said. ""When you're Scottish, [that's] not unusual. A kilt is your tuxedo so she loves that and she's Chinese so for us, we're going to do a sort of fusion of her heritage and my heritage.""
When asked what you wear under a kilt, Scott replied, ""I think you know the answer to that!""
His pro dance partner Slater told reporters that she and Farber have set a date noting that ""Things have been picking up this last week. I'm in the process of sorting out invitations. We're about to go on [the upcoming ""DWTS"" tour] so I'm going to be like crazy strange bridezilla for doing my wedding planning on tour which is going to be difficult, but we're going to make it work.""
""DWTS"" fans were thrilled in October 2016 when Farber proposed to Slater during the live show . He got down on one knee with a dazzling ring during the broadcast and, of course, Slater said yes to her longtime fellow dancer beau who's been paired with such stars as Snooki and gymnast Simone Biles. Farber isn't competing this season.
Slater plansto have fellow ""DWTS"" pros in her bridal party, saying, ""We're not going to be that posh, elegant wedding. I want it to be a party of love and have all our friends there and we're going to focus a lot on the entertainment. I want to surprise Sasha. We want it to be crazy!""
Scott said as he's rehearsed with Slater, they've joked about a double wedding.
That would be an interesting idea, particularly because Scott famously co-stars with his identical twin brother Jonathan on their hit HGTV show while Slater has a fraternal twin sister, Kelly.
Scott joked, ""We talked about it. It's still in the works. What we might just do is let Linda and Emma go and plan half of it and Sasha and I will take it up, we'll claim the other half, and then we'll merge.""
But he quipped that they won't get married at the same ceremony because, ""I don't want her and Sasha to upstage me in my first dance with Linda.""
Neither Scott nor Slater wants their wedding to be televised.
The ""Property Brothers"" star noted, ""For me, it's all about family and family time. I don't get a lot of time because I'm on the road all the time and so they're first and foremost to me and [Linda and I are] going to do our wedding in Europe in the spring and that's exciting.""
But he added that afterwards, ""I'm sure we're going to share lots of photos, lots of videos and stuff"" with fans.",ok
