gossipcop-910068,https://variety.com/2018/music/news/donald-glover-retiring-childish-gambino-grammys-1202679904/,Grammys: Donald Glover Confirms He’s Retiring Childish Gambino – Variety,958051919536316420	958052467287216130	958053556115968006	958053891895152646	958054403147055104	958062427026767872	958071707331387395	958071775731974144	958077296283328513	958084397516771328	958092636669095936	958129664412868609	958129680288309249	958129679789109248	958129686802042880	958129726954135552	958129986032062469	958130153154076672	958130166231945217	958130165862797314	958130169302142976	958130217637306369	958130236465573889	958130235698016256	958130255646134274	958130417508474880	958130432893177856	958130437926383618	958130449649369090	958130457484414978	958130476761387009	958130483233255424	958130551004782593	958130653517811714	958130686338174976	958130684698267660	958130732257497095	958130750091681797	958226606803202048	958863739176017923	959033696882970625	959038637202698240	959046928062406656	959051975437451264	959054998092107776	959055248076759042	959055987415142400	959056264201428995	959061530217238528	959063540773597184	959069101212782592	959070104788127744,0,variety.com,72,"Despite his five Grammy Award nominations this year, Donald Glover confirms he still plans to retire his stage name, Childish Gambino .
Last June during his performance at the Governors Ball Music Festival in New York City, Glover announced that his upcoming album will be his last. Backstage at the 2018 Grammys, he elaborated on his decision.
“I stand by that. I’m really appreciative of this. I’m making another project right now,” he said. “But I like endings, I think they’re important to progress.”
He continued, “I think if a lot of things had death clauses in them, we wouldn’t have a lot of problems in the world, to be honest. I think ending are good because they force things to get better.”
Glover scored one win at the Grammys for best traditional R&B performance for “Redbone.” His album, “Awaken, My Love,” was nominated for both album and urban contemporary album of the year, while “Redbone” was nominated for record of the year and best R&B song.
He performed “Terrified,” along with 9-year-old J.D. McCrary during the 60th annual show. The two are starring alongside each other in the live-action remake of “The Lion King,” where Glover is set to portray Simba and McCrary as young Simba.
In September, Glover took home an Emmy for acting and directing for his acclaimed FX show “Atlanta.”",ok
