gossipcop-877072,https://www.avclub.com/longtime-composer-alf-clausen-has-been-fired-from-the-s-1798639971,Longtime composer Alf Clausen has been fired from The Simpsons,902988019912896513	902988043950448640	902988333407711236	902988364579778560	902989751581515776	902990338301755393	902990375966707712	903007999773609989	903008435410690048	903009341137092608	903009726132248577	903009725687652352	903010952488128519	903010957420630026	903117026184409089	903125149263769600	903147297332224001	903154102263316480	903154411907710976	903188111110406145	903188409069559809	903246762818850816	903320350389280768	903321667497205760	903322403240947712	903323338117967873	903323729056419840	903324250324520960	903325616920870912	903325627457175552	903326925887700992	903327517402157057	903327876686204928	903328257566756864	903329036398497793	903329332638220288	903330930957312000	903331773538553856	903332227903344642	903332744511533057	903334424246411265	903338288127365122	903339302372900866	903340846208180224	903346633378816001	903351177710067713	903352398428553216	903356243267395584	903356242654937088	903356245574221824	903357530671390720	903358750718754816	903361814746079233	903371587365126144	903379200207355905	903379202950475776	903379290816905217	903379406315511813	903379481720758274	903379507448557568	903379679750606849	903379698264178688	903379708150239232	903379729826373633	903379747631181824	903379913352327168	903379920595902464	903379918700064773	903379934223245313	903379984554889217	903379990280101888	903380019451441152	903380082315624448	903380175039209472	903380178470141953	903380207066914819	903380265040523268	903380273852583936	903380328156409856	903380325497221120	903380470615957504	903421457211899904	903425515998126080	903491162857603072	903777273815240705	904012545979273216	904051318117072896	904068412854460416	904069166231113733	904072713433747461	904074215204278274	904075458916036612	904075707709628417	904078983200997376	904080257996783617	904081496373436416	904081552115736576	904085522490019840	904091314211495936	904091565181870081	904094108494508032	904094127062691841	904637661125730304	904638321367842816,0,avclub.com,62,"After 27 years of making jaunty cartoon music for The Simpsons , longtime composer Alf Clausen has been fired from the show. That’s according to Variety , which reports that Simpsons producer Richard Sakai recently called Clausen and told him that the show is looking for “a different kind of music,” so someone different will be scoring the series from now on. Considering how omnipresent and iconic Clausen’s score has been, though, it seems likely that any “different kind of music” will be a huge change for The Simpsons .
Variety expects that this decision was because of money, which has been a regular issue for the show over the last few years, with the story saying that the costs for scoring the series “routinely run into the millions of dollars per year” because of Matt Groening’s insistence that it use a 35-piece orchestra for every episode. It’s unclear which cheap scab will be hired to replace Clausen, but Danny Elfman’s famous Simpsons theme will most likely stick around.
Clausen won two Emmy awards for his work on The Simpsons , and he has been nominated 21 times on top of that. His final episode was the season 28 finale , which aired earlier this year.",ok
gossipcop-867756,https://www.vogue.co.uk/gallery/celebrity-skincare-regimes,24 Celebrities On Their Skincare Routines,887662579601948673	887662869910884352	887663639787966464	887664183621189632	887664192483844096	887665326212689920	887665706761940994	887666800325873665	887666798060912641	887666946191347713	887667028630417412	887667447519748097	887668064019501057	887668434535723008	887671105758138369	887674605586046976	887676296544780288	887683056269701121	887699278797438976	887699387685769218	887699393167728640	887699439644688385	887699460448497666	887699503826030592	887699547589406720	887699630045233152	887699660881752067	887699740191805440	887699893627875333	887699897520201731	887699966306775042	887699965870583808	887699972036206593	887699992277905409	887700006085505024	887700024746016769	887700083332046852	887700143692185600	887700161878740992	887700162826694657	887700230455644163	887700234855477253	887700270985203714	887700400819843073	887700455781957632	887711601838743555	887725862493224961	887782583135866880	887817302971789312	887830795892686848,0,vogue.co.uk,41,"Over the years, British Vogue has spoken to an array of actors, models, musicians and other famous faces about their beauty secrets and the advice they've picked up along the way. Here, we collate all the details on celebrity skincare routines, from Susan Sarandon's laid-back approach to Margot Robbie's love of deep cleansing and Clémence Poésy's French pharmacy favourites.
At the Cannes Film Festival she wore her hair straight, with a side parting.
""I like to moisturise my skin with an oil, morning and night. And I’ll do masks too, usually I’ll choose a clay mask, they’re really good. In my work I’ve also really learned how important it is to clean your skin before you go to bed. I’ve been using L’Oréal Paris’s Fine Flowers Cleansing Cream, which I love."" Read the full interview with Borges here .
""Every day I exfoliate because from the shows there’s a lot of make-up, sweat and dirt on my skin and just from being in a lot of different places - a lot of different airports - you have to really deeply clean your skin. So I exfoliate every day, and I use this honey moisturiser that I got. Then sometimes I’ll do face masks and clay masks and honey masks."" Read the full interview with Cabello here .
""I always take my make-up off no matter how tired I am. Daily I use Tracie Martyn Amla Purifying Cleanser. It’s very fresh, gently scented and really deep cleans the face and neck. And it’s fast, no fuss. And I like using a good flat facial sponge to make sure it's truly clean. I get quite dry skin so occasionally I use an old favourite of mine, Lancôme Toner Comfort, and then I slather up with Advanced Genefique Sensitive. This is my two-for-the-price-of-one product! It combines two serum concentrates with a vitamin E boost, all in one bottle. Shake, slather, done. It’s really hydrating and fresh and fast to use."" Read the full interview with Winslet here .
Lively wore her hair in long, soft curls, swept back from her face for CinemaCon in Las Vegas.
""I had really bad skin until I was 24 and up until then I did everything under the sun to it. Then one day I thought I would try to leave it and that's what suited it better. That's also why I always want to wear as little make-up as possible when I am not working. When I'm filming, I always have a breakout as we have to cake the make-up on. I think it needs a break every now and again to be able to breathe. Since having a baby and being over 30, it's also getting dry for the first time. That's why I have started to use oils and moisturisers over the past few years."" Read the full interview with Knightley here .
""'Regime', like 'skincare regime' is one of those words which I haven't really integrated into my life. Things that I do regularly are to put on my sunblock, keep my face clean and use moisturiser. I'm starting to educate myself to the wide range of products L'Oréal has [since becoming a brand spokesperson]. I love the Age Perfect range, that's the big one for me I think. You could stand a spoon in the moisturiser and it would stay upright it's so thick, and you could practically eat it it's so rich."" Read the full interview with Sarandon here .
""I’ll maybe do a lip, but for every day I use a lot of mascara. And sometimes I’ll do a bit of liner - I like big open eyes, babydoll-ish. L’Oréal Paris’s Voluminous Lash Paradise Mascara is so perfect and also it’s in pink packaging. It’s so cute."" Read the full interview with Fanning here .
“I love statement bold lips for an event, so maybe a bright or dark red. And I’m not big on eyeshadow but I love liner and a great lash.” Read the full interview with Kloss here .
""I don't really have a regime, it’s the bare essentials! I use a face wash and then sometimes I use a serum but usually I go straight for the Decorté AQ Meliority Intensive Cream, and I’ll add a couple of drops of the Decorté Vitality Tincture too. It works. You really see the difference. I gave it to all the girls for Christmas and they loved it."" Read the full interview with Moss here .
""My regime is pretty straightforward. I’m lucky that I have fairly good genes and my skin is pretty good, but I’m always careful to wash my face and cleanse it. I live in New York City and it’s so cold in the winter and so hot in the summer, plus I fly a lot, so my skin is and always has been more on the dry side. So I do a lot of moisturising. I especially love the Blue Therapy range from Biotherm - there are great oils and creams and they’re super-rich. I kind of play around with little bits and pieces of the whole range. I do that in the morning and pretty much the same at night – there’s a great night cream in the range too."" Read the full interview with Turlington-Burns here .
""I try to keep my skincare routine very simple and don’t put too much on my face. If I’ve been going out a lot, I like to do a lot of different face masks. For a daily cleanse, I use African Black Soap - it’s very pure and keeps my face clean. Afterwards, I tone with a mixture of water and tea tree oil. I try to make sure that everything I use is hypo-allergenic and natural. I love Eau Thermale Avène’s Skin Recovery Cream. It’s the only one I’ve used which doesn’t make me break me out and completely calms down my skin."" Read the full interview with Harlow here .
""I really like the La Mer Cleansing Gel. Then Dior has a really gentle exfoliator - Instant Gentle Exfoliant - that I really love. I never used to use elixirs or anything like that, but Dior’s Prestige line has this Le Nectar De Nuit serum which is amazing, it has this incredible rose scent. My skin just loves that. Then I’ll end with a really great moisturiser. I like Dior’s L’Or De Vie La Crème moisturiser, or the Prestige La Crème. Then if it’s winter and really, really cold, I’ll use Crème De La Mer."" Read the full interview with Theron here .
""I use Avène because I think it's quite light and gentle, it's not perfumed or anything like that. And I don't go in the sun, I'm not a tanner at all. In fact I'm quite scared of the sun, so it's SPF50 all over. And when I'm really hungover I like to lie in my bed with a Korean sheet mask on my face."" Read the full interview with Campbell here .
""I like toners. I’m all about a good astringent toner before I put my moisturiser on. I can’t just put moisturiser on - I have breakouts because I work out. I don’t actually get zits or acne, I just get these red marks where it’s, like, about to break out and it shows up like a rash on the side of my face. So I like for it to feel like zingy clean with astringent. Then I like La Mer - I think it’s beautiful - but I haven’t found an astringent that goes with La Mer yet, actually. I usually use Elizabeth Arden astringent, or I use Neutrogena… I use a couple of different astringents actually. And I love to play with products too."" Read the full interview with Spears here .
""I'm a big cleanse, tone and moisturise every night and morning kind of person. I take really good care of my skin actually and I love products, I love Kate Somerville, Liz Earle - stuff that feels really natural and light on your skin. I never sleep with my make-up on. Even when I'm really drunk I wake up with a washed face. It's a miracle sometimes, I don't know how it happens. I like feeling like my skin can breathe."" Read the full interview with James here .
“To switch my make-up up at night I’ll add a lip. It transforms your whole look - you can be wearing a plain outfit and then a strong lip completely changes the vibe. I’ll usually go for red or like a brownish shade. I like a strong highlight too, at night you can proper whack it on and be a glowing goddess.” Read the full interview with Jama here .
""Because I wear a lot of make-up for work it's really important to keep my skin clean after work so I use a great natural face wash with tea tree oil and green tea. I use organic coconut oil to take my make-up off, I also add it to my smoothies to keep my skin glowing. It's a great all-round natural beauty product. The main thing my mum taught me was that you can never be too young to start taking care of your skin. No matter how tired I am, I will never sleep in my make-up."" Read the full interview with Swanepoel here .",ok
gossipcop-904699,https://www.etonline.com/inside-golden-globes-2018-after-parties-how-stars-cut-loose-93823,Inside the Golden Globes 2018 After Parties: How the Stars Cut Loose,950366261749403648	950366524157644801	950367151264804864	950368590544257025	950369682623750144	950370996820856832	950377321940307971	950378318267695104	950379096659320832	950379783883542531	950405892960333824	950436008264265729	950436874727944192	950659473617637376,0,etonline.com,68,"For many celebrities, the night was just getting started when host Seth Meyers wrapped up the 75th Annual Golden Globe Awards on Sunday.
Following the show, ET hit up the most exclusive after-parties in Hollywood, and got a firsthand look at how the stars mingle when the cameras are off.
Here's what went down when the real partying began!
Amazon Studios' Golden Globes Celebration presented by Audi at Beverly Hilton Hotel: Bromances and Dances
Matt Damon and Chris Hemsworth inspired some major friendship goals when they greeted one another with a hug while at Amazon's after-party presented by Audi at the Beverly Hilton Hotel.
Hemsworth was seen shimmying to The Weeknd's ""I Can't Feel My Face"" and chatting with friends, while Damon and his wife, Luciana Barroso, took to the dance floor to cut loose.
Meanwhile, The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel star Rachel Brosnahan mingled at the party with her Golden Globe in hand and a champagne in another. She was later seen cuddling up to her date on one of the couches.
Kate Beckinsale was a fan favorite at the event. Mobbed by party goers for photos, the actress happily stopped to pose with anyone that asked her.
As for Paris Hilton and her fiance, Chris Zylka, they had a look of love when they arrived to the event. The 36-year-old socialite was seen showing off her new engagement ring that she was wearing over lace gloves.
Also spotted at the bash was Modern Family star Sarah Hyland and her boyfriend, Wells Adams. The two were seen kissing while waiting to get into the video booth, and Hyland even danced a little bit to Justin Bieber's ""Sorry.""
InStyle and Warner Bros. Golden Globe Post-Party at Beverly Hilton Hotel: Major Star Sightings
A slew of stars hit up this party on Sunday night!
Even before the A-listers stepped into the soiree, they were letting loose in the elevator. Pregnant supermodel Miranda Kerr even did a little jig while putting her baby bump on display.
The women of Big Little Lies , Reese Witherspoon, Laura Dern, Zoe Kravitz and Shailene Woodley, were seen toasting at a table together following the show's big win. Kerry Washington, Emma Watson and Michelle Williams were also at their table, and all sang along with the actresses to Madonna.
Witherspoon didn't stay seated for very long. The 41-year-old actress made sure to say hello to Orange Is the New Black star Laverne Cox.
Mariah Carey showed up to the soiree with boyfriend Bryan Tanaka, and at one point in the evening, Salma Hayek was seen dancing in front of the singer's table. Carey seemed very smitten with Tanaka, and happily posed for photos with fans who stopped at her table.
Henry Cavill made friends with a fans! The Man of Steel star asked a woman to do a tequila shot with him after she praised his work.
At another table, Allison Janney was celebrating her Golden Globes win with a large group of people. Seated on the upper part of the booth, the actress was moving along to the beat of the music.
Hulu's 2018 Golden Globes After Party at Beverly Hilton Hotel: Handmaids Hit the Dance Floor
The stars of The Handmaid's Tale were seen celebrating the show's big wins on the dance floor! An eyewitness at the party saw Elisabeth Moss and Alexis Bledel busting a move to Luis Fonsi's ""Despacito"" and Taylor Swift's ""End Game.""
Seth Meyers' Golden Globe After-Party at The h.wood Group's Poppy, presented by Beats By Dre: J.T. Brings the Fun
