which seem to be influencing Lady Gaga these days), Billboard revisits 25 of Cher’s most outrageous outfits.
From her flower-child early days in Sonny & Cher to her signature biker-gymnast onesies (which seem to be influencing Lady Gaga these days), Billboard revisits 25 of Cher’s most outrageous outfits.
Cher and Sonny Bono first became famous as a novelty act. And while their clothes were textural and proportioned in ways that were unconventional at the time, Cher’s straight hair also made a statement–most women were still wearing beehives.
Cher perpetually pushed boundaries when it came to how much skin she revealed (she famously drew CBS’ ire for exposing her naval on air). And while this versions of this gown have since surfaced on red carpets–it was an extremely daring move at the time.
The Native-American goddess-inspired look has been a staple throughout Cher’s career, and was most recently re-worked for her show in Vegas.
INGLEWOOD, CA – 1974: Entertainer Cher performs as ringmaster at the opening day of the Ringling Brothers Circus as part of a celebrtiy event in 1974 in Inglewood, California. (Photo by Michael Ochs Archives/Getty Images)
Mackie, a master of proportions and period-dressing, could easily take away the sequins and transform Cher into a Gone With The Wind southern belle for television.
Liberace (left) gave Cher (pictured in character as ‘Laverne’) a tour of his Hollywood Hills mansion for an episode of the Sonny And Cher Show in January 1974. Forty years later, the costume is still being emulated for Halloween.
Cher in a semi-transparent outfit with a feathered headdress for the television variety show 'The Sonny and Cher Comedy Hour' in 1972. (Photo by CBS Photo Archive/Getty Images)
While the rest of Hollywood arrived to the Academy Awards in tuxedos and straightforward evening gowns, Cher brought the color and energy of a tropical island princess to the carpet in 1972.
Title: Romantic and Glamorous Hollywood Design Exhibition Caption: Cher (Photo by Ron Galella/WireImage)
Cher poses for a Fashion Session in a Bob Mackie Creation on April 9, 1978 in Los Angeles.
Bejeweled unitards with criss-crossing down the front like the one Cher wears here, have become a pop-star staple for artists like Demi Lovato and J.Lo.
For the 1978 Disco Convention Banquet in New York, Cher was a vision in gold.
Cher poses for a Fashion Session in a Bob Mackie Creation on April 9, 1978 in Los Angeles.
Cher poses for an Album Cover Session for 'The Prisoner' on Casablanca Records in June 1979 in Los Angeles.
Title: 58th Annual Academy Awards Caption: Cher (Photo by Jim Smeal/WireImage) Date created: 24 Mar 1986
Title: 60th Annual Academy Awards Caption: Cher (Photo by Barry King/WireImage) Date created: 11 Apr 1988
Cher channeled Cleopatra at a 1988 Halloween Party.
This ultra-sexy black biker-esque body suit is designed to accentuate Cher in all the right places.
Title: The 70th Annual Academy Awards – Red Carpet Caption: Cher at the Shrine Auditorium in Los Angeles, California (Photo by Steve Granitz/WireImage) Date created: 23 Mar 1998
Cher took her hair to new heights in 2000, with an incredible mohawk-meets-tribal-inspired headpiece.
Cher looked regal in a mirrored and fur-trimmed coat at a 2000 Australian performance.
A different kind of sparkle, Cher opted for silver pants that were paired with red sunglasses for a goth-meet-retro vibe.
Channeling “The King” at VH1 “Divas” in 2002, the stage look was a completely new direction for Cher.
Cher is a master of the style mash-up. Only she could pull off the goth look with lots of old-west fringe at the 2002 Billboard Music Awards.
