gossipcop-889683,https://www.seventeen.com/celebrity/celebrity-couples/a19747317/khloe-kardashian-tristan-thompson-relationship-timeline/,Khloe Kardashian and Tristan Thompson Relationship Timeline,,0,seventeen.com,59,"Seventeen picks products that we think you'll love the most. We may earn commission from the links on this page.
Since Khloé Kardashian and Tristan Thompson started dating in 2016, the couple has been consistently on-again, and off-again. While the pair is not together anymore following the news that Tristan fathered a child with Maralee Nichols , things are said to be “okay” between the reality star and NBA player. According to reports, their focus is primarily on “co-parenting” their four-year-old daughter, True Thompson, who they welcomed in 2018, and the new baby boy they welcomed in August. If you’re having trouble keeping track of all their highs and lows and drama, here is a complete timeline of Khloé and Tristan’s relationship.
Khloé and Tristan came together to showcase their baby boy's face for the first time on Hulu's reality series The Kardashians . In a preview for next week's upcoming episode obtained by People , Tristan walked into a room holding baby Tatum as he thanked Khloé, Kim Kardashian, and Kris Jenner for their support. ""Thank you so much, from me and my family, I don't know what I would do without you guys right now,"" he said.
In the latest episode of The Kardashians , Khloé opened up about the real reason she forgave ex Tristan Thompson for his multiple cheating scandals over the years. The 39-year-old Good American founder went to dinner with sister Kim Kardashian and Scott Disick at Casa Vega in Sherman Oaks, California, Scott asked Khloé if Tristan had any chances of reconciling their relationship. ""No, no chances,"" Khloé said.
Scott then reassured Khloe that he ""would support"" her if she decided to get back with Tristan, to which she responded that she was ""totally fine"" with Tristan and that she ""just don't have the energy for issues.""
""Yeah, I forgive Tristan,"" she explained in a confessional, noting that it ""doesn't mean I forget what he's done."" She continued, ""I forgive Tristan for me because I've got to let that s--t go. I need to for myself. I can't move on with my life if I'm holding onto this bulls--t.""
Things were so tense between Khloé and Tristan when they welcomed their son in August 2022 that the reality star reportedly gave their son Tatum the last name Kardashian instead of the Los Angeles Lakers star's last name Thompson. According to TMZ , a source revealed that Khloé reportedly had a change of heart and legally changed his last name to Thompson sometime later. The source also revealed that Tatum wasn't the baby's first name but did not disclose Khloé and Tristan's original name for their baby boy.
Just in case you need a refresher, the on-again, off-again couple welcomed their son via a surrogate months after news broke that Tristan got another woman pregnant while they were still together.
Khloé is officially moving on from Tristan, and she isn't looking back. During the newest episode of the Hulu series The Kardashians , the Good American founder explained to her mom Kris Jenner, that although she and Tristan were on good terms, they had no plans of getting back together. ""Tristan and I, we always get along great. Him and I have a great friendship relationship, we get along fine, and for my kids, I will put anything to the side,"" she said. ""What's done is done, so what would I still be holding on to something for? I don't need to punish him because I'm not getting back with him.""
Kris recounted a ""really cute"" memory of Tristan eating breakfast with their 5-year-old daughter True at Khloé's house, but Khloé was adamant about the two of them doing what's best for their children. ""Yeah if I'm not here when I'm not around, he's here,"" she replied. ""I would rather him be here than the nanny."" Despite their co-parenting relationship, the mom of two made it clear that she's done pursuing a romantic relationship with him. ""There's still boundaries, I'm definitely putting my foot down around a lot of things. No one's just here chilling if there's no kids involved.""
Nine months after Khloé and Tristan’s baby boy was born via surrogacy, his name has finally been unveiled. During the season 3 premiere of Hulu’s The Kardashians , Khloé shared that her son’s name is Tatum. ❤️
The reality star previously revealed that her second baby’s name started with a T, and her bestie Malika Haqq appeared to divulge his moniker just a few days ago on Instagram, but this is the first time that Khloé herself has confirmed his name. As she said in the premiere of the reality series, “Naming a human is really hard.”
Khloé Kardashian has had enough of online reports that she's reconciled with Tristan Thompson. The Good American co-founder left a lengthy caption on a fan page that reposted a screenshot from popular celeb gossip blog Deuxmoi's Instagram Story that read, ""Kim supporting Tristan at the Lakers game… what is going on? 🫠.""
Khloé wrote, ""Stop pushing this narrative. It's tiring. But I suppose You guys will continue the narrative you want regardless of what I say so what's the point."" The mom of two says the rumors are ""exhausting"" but says she ""learned people will only understand to the level of their own perception."" The Kardashians star continued, "" Most are stuck at believing the lies because it's the narrative they want to fuel. Have fun."" She also explained the truth behind her sister Kim Kardashian's recent appearance at several of the Los Angeles Lakers playoff games, where Tristan played. ""Some things are just as simple as they seem. A family member supporting another family member ESPECIALLY during a difficult time in life,"" Khloe said, hinting at the recent death of Tristan's mother.
She followed up with an example of how she continues to show up for her sister's exes despite their relationships having ended. ""Example.... just how I support Scott and will forever support him. He's my brother. It's just not on an NBA stage. Sad new world, If there's no photos people think it really didn't happen but yes, I see Scott often. Somethings really are just as they are.""
The fan page posted a screenshot of Khloe's comment and issued an apology, and she replied, ""Thanks babe!""
Oops! 😅 It seems like Tristan has been subtly keeping up with his ex through Instagram. The NBA player accidentally revealed his hand when he viewed a series of IG Story polls featuring lots of photos of Khloé from fan account @updatekhloee .
""Hello Tristan,"" wrote @updatekhloee over a screenshot obtained by The Sun . Tristan's username, @realtristan13 , along with his verified Blue Checkmark, were clearly visible at the top of the list of 76 viewers. We wonder how many other fan accounts he's currently stalking...
On Easter Sunday, the Los Angeles Lakers announced that NBA player Tristan has officially joined their team. Their official Instagram page posted a pic of Tristan in the iconic gold and violet jersey, writing, ""OFFICIAL: Tristan Thompson and Shaquille Harrison are Los Angeles Lakers."" Per E! News , the basketball player's ex, Khloé Kardashian, subtly showed her support by liking the announcement.
ICYMI, Tristan previously played for the Cleveland Cavaliers, Chicago Bulls, and Boston Celtics and Khloé would constantly sit courtside to support him when they were together.
Khloé and Tristan have kept the name of their seven-month-old son under wraps since his birth via surrogate in August 2022. The proud mom of two appeared on The Jennifer Hudson Show , where she revealed her son's name is similar to his sister, True, and father, Tristan, because it starts with a ""T.""
According to the reality star-turned-entrepreneur, she didn't pick a name out at birth because she ""wanted to meet him and feel him out a little bit."" Khloé revealed her plan to reveal her baby boy's name when her family's Hulu series, The Kardashians, premieres its third season on May 25, but she ""didn't know it was going to be this far out."" Plus, she's hoping her four-year-old daughter True can keep his name under wraps until then. ""Now I'm just like if my daughter outs me... I'm screwed.""
Tristan is reportedly on a mission to win his on-again-off-again girlfriend back. According to Us Weekly , the NBA star ""hasn't completely given up hope,"" while his ex has ""made it clear"" that she has no plans of getting back with him. ""He knows they're always going to be in each other's lives because of their children. But that doesn't mean he hasn't been trying,"" the insider told Us . ""At this point, he feels like all he can do is be the best father to their kids that he can and show Khloé over time that he's there for their family. He is so happy he was able to find a home right around the corner from them because they're his priority. He just wants to be there for his kids.""
The same day this report was published, the on-again-off-again couple-turned-neighbors were spotted with their two children in a drive-through at a McDonald's in Rialto, California. According to TMZ , the duo ordered ""a LOT of food,"" including child-friendly happy meals.
Khloé and Tristan have gone from co-parents to neighbors. According to Page Six , the NBA star purchased a $12.5 million, 10,584-square-foot home three doors down from the one his ex shares with their two children in Hidden Hills, California. The Sun reports that Tristan signed the dotted line on the house in December 2022.
