Khloé is setting the record straight about her relationship status. The mother of two took to social media on Sunday amid rumors that she reunited with her ex. During a Twitter chat with her fans, the Good American founder was asked about ""her man,"" and she replied, ""Who has time for a man lol I have a 6 month old baby and True and I are sickly codependent on one another.""  Khloé added, ""Ha! I secretly love it. No but for real…. No man right now…. He’s in my prayers too ha!""
On Sunday, Tristan took to Instagram to remember his late mother, Andrea Thompson. The NBA star shared a carousel post of images with his mother, his three brothers, his ex Khloe and his daughter True. ""It has been one month since you’ve been gone. I’m in disbelief. I'm in the deepest part of sorrow & grief,"" Tristan began. ""My soul is empty as I come to terms that my biggest supporter/superhero is gone. I cannot thank you enough for always being a woman of faith, being one of God's warriors, fighting back with whatever the world threw our way.""
The father of three also addressed his public shortcomings and promised to use his mother's memory as inspiration to become a better man. ""All I can say is, Im sorry mommy for the wrong decisions I've made in my life. I'm sorry for the embarrassment &pain,"" he wrote. ""You raised me better than what I was able to show you. But I have also learned sorry is not enough. Actions speak louder than words. So I wont just say sorry. Stay tuned to the ways I will show the world what an amazing son you raised. I will show you that even when we fall & make mistakes, we get back up. You are my motivation. Stand beside me as I become the man I know you always believed in. I'm going to make you proud, I promise!""
He later thanked his late mother for the sacrifices she made for him and his siblings and promised to take care of his youngest brother. ""Amari is going to be taken care of,"" he wrote. ""I’ll protect him, love him &do anything in the world to make sure he’s ok.""
Khloé took to Instagram on Thursday to share some empowering quotes about love, loss, peace, and gratitude. “Work on yourself and vibe alone for a while... every season don’t need company,” one message read. “A woman that found peace instead of revenge can never be bothered,” another declared.
