gossipcop-930011,https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/country/8469916/cole-swindell-all-of-it-video-behind-the-scenes-clip,Cole Swindell Shows Fans How His 'All of It' Video Storyline Reached a Happy Ending: Exclusive,989852854528524288	989853026826452992	989853631905230849	989855538543583232	989855735608639489	989855819113160711	989856218410823680	989856272995487746	989856644518445056	989864544641077253	989871610982154241	989879314052071425	989884419916754944	989892187876872192	989899817336754176	989919434004295680,0,billboard.com,94,"Since Cole Swindell burst onto the scene with his 2013 breakout hit, “Chillin’ It,” his track record has been unbelievable. Four of the country star’s first seven singles hit No. 1 on Country Airplay , with the other three reaching No. 2 on the chart. Along with owning the country radio market, Swindell has carved out a reputation as a rising live act, and he’ll continue his Reason To Drink Tour with part two this fall: The Reason To Drink… Another Tour, which kicks off October 4 in Tuscaloosa, Alabama, with Dustin Lynch and Lauren Alaina along for the trek.
Related Quevedo & Kidd Voodoo Talk New Urban Movement: 'One of the Things That Makes Us Unique Is Where We Come From' ADÉLA to Make Late Night Debut With 'Tonight Show' Interview & Performance New Wave Greats The B-52s to Receive Star on Hollywood Walk of Fame: Now That's a 'Cosmic Thing' Explore Cole Swindell See latest videos, charts and news
Swindell will be featuring some new music on his next tour, as his third album ? , All of It , arrives this Friday (Aug. 17). The singer has been teasing fans with videos for four of the set’s songs: “Somebody’s Been Drinking,” “The Ones Who Got Me Here,” “Love You Too Late,” and the romantic title track. The video for “All of It” finishes the story arc that Swindell began in the first clip, and Billboard has an exclusive behind-the-scenes look at how the visual came together.
The video — which was released on Aug. 10 – features Swindell in the kitchen cooking for his love interest, something that he hints may not actually happen off camera. “I’m glad it’s on video, and we’re not actually having to eat it,” the singer quips while on set.
With “All of It” bringing an end to the storyline Swindell has created with his recent videos, the clip for the title track features the same girl from the singer’s All of It video sequence, Alicia. Fans who have followed the storyline will take solace in the fact that the on-screen couple is together again at the end – proving that sometimes, couples don’t “Break Up In The End.”
Swindell will be performing some All of It tracks as part of Billboard ’s Facebook Live series later today (Aug. 15). Tune into Billboard’s Facebook page at 3:30 pm ET, and in the meantime check out behind-the-scenes footage of “All of it” below.
