gossipcop-861352,https://www.celebritynetworth.com/richest-businessmen/paul-nassif-net-worth/,Paul Nassif Net Worth,,0,celebritynetworth.com,21,"Paul Nassif is an American plastic surgeon, entrepreneur, and television personality who has a net worth of $60 million. Paul Nassif is best known for his expertise in facial reconstructive surgery. He gained widespread recognition as a co-host of the hit reality series ""Botched,"" where he helps patients correct failed cosmetic procedures alongside fellow surgeon Dr. Terry Dubrow .
Specializing in rhinoplasty and facial plastic surgery, Nassif built a successful medical practice in Beverly Hills, catering to high-profile clients and individuals seeking complex reconstructive procedures. He has pioneered advanced surgical techniques and is regarded as a leading authority in revision rhinoplasty.
Beyond surgery, Nassif has expanded his career into entrepreneurship. He launched NassifMD Dermaceuticals, a skincare line focused on anti-aging and skin rejuvenation, which has been featured on QVC and gained a global customer base. His business ventures, combined with his television presence, have positioned him as a prominent figure in the aesthetics industry.
In addition to ""Botched,"" Nassif has appeared on reality shows like ""Dr. 90210"" and ""The Real Housewives of Beverly Hills,"" the latter through his previous marriage to Adrienne Maloof . With a combination of surgical expertise, media influence, and business acumen, Paul Nassif continues to be a leading voice in plastic surgery and cosmetic innovation.
Paul S. Nassif, MD, was born on June 6, 1962, in Los Angeles, California. He is Lebanese-American. Nassif attended Loyola High School and the University of Southern California. He graduated in 1974. Nassif studied at Rosalind Franklin University of Medicine and Science/Chicago Medical School for the first two years of his medical education. He graduated from the University of Southern California School of Medicine in 1992, which he attended for the last two years of his general medical education.
Nassif interned in general surgery residency at the University of New Mexico Health Sciences Center. He then had a residency in Otolaryngology-head and neck surgery at the University of New Mexico from 1993 to 1997. In 1998, Dr. Nassif completed a facial plastic and reconstructive surgery fellowship at St. Louis University School of Medicine in 1998.
He is licensed in both California and Nevada and practices facial plastic surgery, specifically rhinoplasty, in Beverly Hills. He sees patients from all over the world. Paul is a member of the American Society for Aesthetic Plastic Surgery.
(Photo by Tibrina Hobson/Getty Images for Mediaplacement )
Dr. Nassif is best known for appearing on the E! series ""Botched,"" which focuses on reversing bad plastic surgery. The show premiered in June 2014 and has aired for six seasons. Dr. Nassif also appeared in the first three seasons of ""The Real Housewives of Beverly Hills"" alongside his now ex-wife, Adrienne Maloof, who was a main cast member. In October 2015, it was announced that an eight-episode spin-off series of ""Botched"" called ""Botched by Nature"" would air. The show premiered on August 9, 2016. Paul has been featured on ""Dr. 90210"" and has appeared on ""NBC Nightly News,"" ""Inside Edition,"" ""CBS Healthbeat,"" ""Entertainment Tonight,"" ""Today,"" ""Good Morning America,"" and ""Extra.""
Nassif also teaches at the University of Southern California and the University of California, Los Angeles, schools of medicine. Nassif has his own skincare line, Nassif MD Dermaceutical. The skincare line focuses on anti-aging and skin rejuvenation.
Nassif married businesswoman Adrienne Maloof on May 2, 2002. She is a member of the prominent Maloof family . The couple has three sons together. Paul filed for separation from Adrienne in July 2012, saying that she had been physically and verbally abusive toward him in front of their children. Their divorce was finalized on November 8, 2012. Nassif married medical assistant Brittany Pattakos in September 2019. In June 2020, they announced they were expecting their first child together.
In 2015, Dr. Nassif paid $4.9 million for property in LA's Bel-Air neighborhood. He proceeded to construct a 12,000-square-foot luxurious mansion. Paul listed this home for sale in July 2022 for $30 million. He ultimately sold it for $20.4 million in June 2023. The sale was an auction, so after fees, Nassif's take was around $18.5 million . A month before listing the Bel-Air mansion, Nassif paid $14 million for a home in Dana Point, California. Here are two videos of Paul's mansion, one posted by Nassif himself in October 2022 and the second posted by the auction house that ultimately handled the sale:",ok
