He's already well-accustomed to working the red carpet, despite being only 10 months old.
But DJ Khaled's adorable baby son Asahd well and truly stole the show at the MTV Video Music Awards at The Forum in Inglewood, California, on Sunday night.
The tot looked incredible as he sported a custom-made Gucci suit to match his record producer father's look.
Cutie: DJ Khaled's adorable baby son Asahd, 10 months, well and truly stole the show at the MTV Video Music Awards at The Forum in Inglewood, California, on Sunday night
Khaled, 41, rocked a Gucci athleisure outfit while his boy wore a similar suit by the same design house as Khaled announced: 'My son is a don!'
Sporting a funky black, purple, pink, and white Japanese graffiti design pullover, the I'm The One hitmaker was joined by his fiance Nicole Tuck, 38.
The New Orleans native added to the casual look with loose navy track pants that hung low on his waist.
Khaled rocked black Nike Air Jordans and a few dazzling accessories with a diamond bracelet, bedazzled pinky ring, and a large silver wristwatch.
Living the life: The tot looked incredible as he sported a custom-made Gucci suit to match his record producer father's look
His fiancee of one year looked sophisticated chic in a classic black dress that cut just above her knees.
But the star of the show was Asahd who looked adorable in the black suit with colorful dragons that played off his father's sartorial choice.
According to his father, Gucci 'came by the house' and tailored the look for Khaled, who’s nominated for four VMAS.
This isn't the first time Asahd took the crown for best dressed at an awards show.
Father-son fashions: Khaled, 41, rocked a Gucci athleisure outfit while his boy wore a similar suit by the same design house as Khaled announced: 'My son is a don!'
Oh baby: The father-son duo later appeared on stage with Katy Perry and a prosthetic baby during the awards show
