gossipcop-849054,https://www.celebritynetworth.com/richest-businessmen/richest-designers/lilly-ghalichi-net-worth/,Lilly Ghalichi Net Worth,861333599215263744	861333599043297280	861333616118321153	861333618635018240	861333641238122497	861333882020474881	861334104595472384	861334355788025856	861334375996071936	861334377942327296	861334382199558145	861334389451440128	861334389375909890	861334389367521281	861334387723444224	861334389896077313	861334397521244161	861334438730444800	861334850321739776	861335236923187200	861335235778064384	861335244388958208	861335250810454016	861335790835597312	861336277316251648	861336382857371648	861336412272173056	861336540454297600	861336830528163840	861336893702778880	861337081158696961	861338251163910144	861338653318152192	861338680492826624	861339031073734656	861340011513470981	861340069990469632	861340076822933504	861340143772454918	861340181357449216	861340515500818432	861340675874410496	861341404663914497	861347334290014208	861349188176564224	861349446570827776	861349445652201472	861349451507523584	861349448152166404	861349454405812224	861349454024015872	861349453948526592	861349452791005184	861349466191740928	861349964382969856	861364260458377216	861365018474024960	861367418861441025	861372698957578241	861387848531849217	861404656672456704	861431521428684800	861431521235750913	861431521030266880	861431520862453760	861431520711421953	861431520606564352	861431525169963008	861431524478013440	861431523634892800	861431523483860994	861431522124939264	861485659701350400	861515301434925056	861696933546651648,0,celebritynetworth.com,24,"Lilly Ghalichi is a Persian-American entrepreneur, attorney, fashion designer, and reality television personality who has a net worth of $50 million. Although she first gained national exposure on Bravo's ""Shahs of Sunset,"" the overwhelming majority of her fortune comes from the beauty industry.
Ghalichi founded Lilly Lashes, a luxury false-eyelash company whose products became popular with celebrities, makeup artists, influencers, and consumers. The brand expanded from direct online sales into major beauty retailers and was acquired by private equity firm Gauge Capital in 2019. Ghalichi continued serving as its founder and public face after the transaction.
She has also launched or participated in businesses involving swimwear, clothing, hair products, cosmetics, hair-growth supplements, and educational seminars for entrepreneurs. Her portfolio has included Have Faith Swimgerie, WantMyLook, HAIRtamin, and Ghalichi Glam.
Ghalichi and her husband, Dara Mir, have also completed tens of millions of dollars in Bel Air real estate transactions. Her net worth reflects company-sale proceeds, continuing business interests, beauty-brand income, endorsements, investments, and property equity rather than her two seasons of reality television.
Neelufar Seyed Ghalichi was born on April 30, 1983, in Houston, Texas. She was raised in a Persian family alongside her siblings, Yassamin and Mohammed.
Ghalichi attended the University of Texas at Austin's Red McCombs School of Business. She later earned her law degree from Loyola Law School in Los Angeles, graduating with honors.
After passing the California bar examination, Ghalichi decided that her strongest interests were in fashion, beauty, and entrepreneurship rather than practicing law full-time.
Her legal and business education later proved valuable as she negotiated manufacturing arrangements, licensing deals, retail agreements, trademarks, and outside investment for her companies.
Ghalichi joined ""Shahs of Sunset"" during its second season. She was introduced as a luxury real estate client of Reza Farahan and quickly became known for her highly styled appearance, elaborate hair and makeup, and ""Persian Barbie"" image.
She appeared alongside Reza, Mercedes ""MJ"" Javid , Golnesa ""GG"" Gharachedaghi , Mike Shouhed , and Asa Soltan Rahmati .
Ghalichi's storylines focused on dating, friendships, family pressure, fashion, and her efforts to build businesses. She remained a principal cast member for seasons two and three before leaving the series.
Although reality television gave her valuable publicity, her Bravo tenure was relatively brief compared with those of the original cast members.
Ghalichi founded Lilly Lashes after struggling to find false eyelashes that created the dramatic, three-dimensional look she wanted. She began developing styles designed to provide greater volume while remaining suitable for professional makeup application.
The company benefited enormously from celebrity adoption and social media. Its lashes were worn by figures including Kim Kardashian , Kylie Jenner , Jennifer Lopez , Lady Gaga , and Rihanna , providing the brand with publicity that would have cost millions of dollars through traditional advertising.
Lilly Lashes expanded into lash adhesives, tools, mascara, and other eye products. Its merchandise was sold online and through major beauty retailers.
In December 2019, Ghalichi sold Lilly Lashes to private equity firm Gauge Capital. Financial terms were not released. Gauge subsequently placed the brand within Performance Beauty Group alongside other beauty businesses.
The transaction transformed Ghalichi from a successful small-business founder into a multimillionaire with liquidity, retained business interests, and continuing influence over the brand.
Before Lilly Lashes became her primary business, Ghalichi created Have Faith Swimgerie, a swimwear line inspired by lingerie. She also launched or promoted clothing, cosmetics, jewelry, hair products, and beauty accessories through the broader Ghalichi Glam platform.
Ghalichi and entrepreneur Leyla Milani co-created HAIRtamin, a line of hair-growth supplements and haircare products. Ghalichi has also sold educational courses and hosted seminars discussing entrepreneurship, branding, social media marketing, and beauty businesses.
Ghalichi married businessman Dara Mir at the Beverly Hills Hotel in May 2017. Mir is an entrepreneur whose business interests have included ergonomic office furniture and real estate.
Their daughter, Alara, was born in September 2018. Their son, Kashton, was born in June 2022.
Ghalichi and Mir have experienced several public separations. Mir filed for divorce in 2019 before withdrawing the case. Ghalichi filed twice in 2020 and dismissed both petitions after the couple reconciled.
She filed for divorce for a fourth time in June 2025, requesting joint custody under the terms of the couple's prenuptial agreement. In July 2026, she dismissed that filing as well, marking another reconciliation.
Mir paid $6.1 million in 2012 for a hillside property in Bel Air. He demolished the existing residence and developed a larger compound on the site.
In April 2020, Ghalichi and Mir paid $19.5 million for the former Bel Air home of automotive executive Lee Iacocca . The roughly 11,000-square-foot property was located near the Bel-Air Country Club and Hotel Bel-Air. After renovating the residence, they sold it in June 2022 for $27.7 million.
In December 2020, Ghalichi purchased Kathy Griffin 's Bel Air mansion for approximately $14 million. The gated estate contains more than 13,000 square feet, eight bedrooms, a theater, wine cellar, underground garage, and infinity pool. Ghalichi later offered the property for sale for $17.2 million. Here is a video tour:",ok
