Contains spoilers for all the Marvel Cinematic Universe films up to and including Avengers: Endgame .
The Marvel Cinematic Universe is full of household names–some pre-established and some that the studio made themselves. This is a franchise with so much star power that even small roles are taken by the likes of Glenn Close and John C. Reilly. Which is its own special kind of shame.
Still, to maintain this level of impressive casting over its long-form storytelling style, Marvel Studios gets most of its cast members on multi-film contracts. We did some digging to find out how many films everyone has left. Where official information is available, we’ve used that as a source. We’ve tried to fill in the gaps with our own guesswork. We’ll keep this incredibly long list up-to-date as we learn more. Given the Avengers: Endgame ending and the potential for some permanent deaths , some major spoilers are ahead…
Films appeared in so far: Iron Man, The Incredible Hulk (cameo), Iron Man 2, The Avengers, Iron Man 3, Avengers: Age Of Ultron, Captain America: Civil War, Spider-Man: Homecoming, Avengers: Infinity War, Avengers: Endgame
The first superhero that Marvel Studios presented us with was Robert Downey Jr. ’s Tony Stark – a casting masterstroke that would become the benchmark for all future Marvel heroes. Given his emotional sendoff , unless Stark returns as a hologram, Endgame appears to be Downey Jr.’s Marvel swansong.
read more – Avengers: Endgame Spoilers, Questions, and Theories
Films appeared in so far: Captain America: The First Avenger, The Avengers, Captain America: The Winter Soldier, Thor: The Dark World (cameo), Avengers: Age Of Ultron, Captain America: Civil War, Spider-Man: Homecoming (cameo), Avengers: Infinity War, Avengers: Endgame
It’s widely known that Chris Evans has expressed an interest in departing superheroics to focus on film directing instead. More recently though he’s been speaking openly about being up for anything that Marvel wants to do with Cap, even though he says he views Avengers: Endgame as a sort of sendoff to his performance. And how could you not? It’s the perfect end to Cap’s MCU journey .
Passing the shield to Falcon at the end of Endgame has major implications for the Falcon and The Winter Soldier TV series coming to Disney+ .
read more – Complete Guide to Marvel and MCU Easter Eggs in Avengers: Endgame
Films appeared in so far: Thor, The Avengers, Thor: The Dark World, Avengers: Age of Ultron, Thor: Ragnarok, Avengers: Infinity War, Avengers: Endgame
Despite not appearing in Civil War , Thor actor Chris Hemsworth was still very much in the Marvel fold. And after Ragnarok and Avengers: Infinity War he can finally be considered an MVP.
further reading – Thor: Ragnarok Complete Easter Egg and Reference Guide
Though Captain America took his hammer in Endgame (Thor still had his trusty Stormbreaker), Thor will likely be hanging around. The film implied future Thor / Guardians of the Galaxy adventures (“Asgardians of the Galaxy”). Hemsworth has expressed interest in doing a Thor 4 past his current contract, complete with a possible return of Taika Waititi as director.
read more: The Internal Logic and Time Travel in Endgame Explained
Films appeared in so far: The Avengers, Iron Man 3 (cameo), Avengers: Age of Ultron , Thor: Ragnarok, Avengers: Infinity War, Avengers Endgame
Mark Ruffalo has made no secret of the six-film deal that Marvel has him on. Seeing as cameos don’t count towards that, he still has two films left, making him among the few stars of the original Avengers movies who is on the hook for continuing past “Phase 3” and Kevin Feige’s fabled Avengers: Endgame finale. This is all great news, however the solo movie is still not happening.
related article: Hulk Movies Marvel Should Make
Films appeared in so far: Iron Man 2, The Avengers, Captain America: The Winter Soldier, Avengers: Age of Ultron, Captain America: Civil War, Avengers: Infinity War, Avengers: Endgame
There’s isn’t an official answer out there on how many Marvel movies Scarlett Johansson ’s Black Widow has left. She said her contract has “morphed” and “mutated” in recent years when Collider asked. We know that she’ll be back for Avengers: Endgame . Kevin Feige has now also (finally) confirmed a Black Widow solo movie is happening after Phase 3, complete with Cate Shortland of the greatly underrated Lore directing. So there seems to be an interest in getting Johansson to reup after her contract is up. Black Widow’s death in Endgame leads us to believe her solo film (we wrote about what to expect in that movie here) will be a prequel.
Films appeared in so far: Thor (cameo), The Avengers, Avengers: Age of Ultron, Captain America: Civil War, Avengers: Endgame
Confirmed upcoming films: Hawkeye (Disney+ TV series)
Jeremy Renner is believed to have a standalone Hawkeye movie on his contract, but that doesn’t seem very close to happening. Further he will only have been in four MCU films in a non-cameo capacity after Endgame , and the standard contract is (at least) six movies. Renner will have a big part in the Marvel TV MCU plans. He’ll portray Haweye on the small screen as Disney+ is developing a Hawkeye TV series in which Clint will pass the mantle of Hawkeye on to Kate Bishop.
Films appeared in so far: Iron Man 2, Iron Man 3, Avengers: Age of Ultron, Captain America: Civil War, Avengers: Infinity War, Avengers: End Game
Without Tony Stark around, we’ll see how the Marvel universe chooses to utlize Rhodey in the future.
