gossipcop-906828,https://www.glamour.com/story/stars-auctioning-off-2018-golden-globes-outfits-timesup,Black Golden Globes Outfits to Be Auctioned Off for the Time's Up Legal Defense Fund,953661215993159681	953661503927934978	953662965517078529	953666121873395712	953673113203453953	953675130206482432	953679868280979457	953685777216544768	953692922666299392	953697900365787137	953700556077322240	953708679202619393	953712631164080128	953720693232824321	953982962130997249,0,glamour.com,84,"Earlier this month, stars including Reese Witherspoon, Tracee Ellis Ross, Mandy Moore, Nicole Kidman, and Laura Dern wore all black to the 2018 Golden Globes in a show of solidarity with survivors of sexual harassment and assault , as well as to raise awareness about anti-workplace harassment initiative Time's Up . Now, they're putting those red carpet outfits up for auction to benefit the movement's legal defense fund. The initiative was announced Wednesday by Time's Up, eBay, and Condé Nast— Glamour 's parent company—who are teaming up to run the auction taking place this Friday.
""We’re thrilled that actors and others in the entertainment industry are leading in this extraordinary way to end the scourge of workplace sexual harassment,” said Fatima Goss Graves, the President and CEO of the National Women’s Law Center, which is in charge of Time's Up's legal defense fund. “Each time they’ve stepped up they’ve inspired more attorneys to join the Time's Up Legal Defense Fund and more individuals to contribute.""
