Ariana Grande and Pete Davidson may not have officially confirmed their engagement yet, but that hasn't stopped the new couple from being open about their love on Instagram .
The 24-year-old singer and 24-year-old Saturday Night Live star have recently shared several videos and photos of their time together on social media, including some that had guest star appearances from THAT ring.
On Friday, Davidson posted a photo showing his and her hands and feet intertwined, with a big engagement ring on display.
Engaged: Ariana Grande, 24, and her 24-year-old Saturday Night Live star lover Pete Davidson shared several videos and photos from their fun day together on Friday
Massive rock: Pete shared a snap of the couple's hands and wrote how great his life is now. Ariana was quick to comment. 'So much better,' she wrote
'U know what you'd dream it be like?' the comedian wrote. 'It's better than that.'
And then Grande commented on the upload.
'So much better,' she wrote. (She also added a heart emoji and a cloud emoji.)
That photo also came with several clips posted on Ariana's Instagram story of the couple having a fun time together, laughing and playing around.
In one video, the comedian is seen showing off his talent, eating an entire Fruit By the Foot with no hands. She then put a clip up of her man dancing silly and making her laugh.
Things got a little more serious, well sort of, when Ari posted a clip of her and Pete driving in the car.
In the video, she's on Snap Chat lip-syncing while sucking on a lollipop. She then pans the camera over to him, and he's hit with a Snap Chat filter that makes him look pretty and puts a flower in his hair.
Two peas in a pod: The couple got engaged recently after just a few weeks of dating
Of course that's cute and all, but that rock on her finger stole everyone's attention.
All of this Instagram PDA hit just hours after the duo's appearance at the 2018 Songwriters Hall of Fame Induction & Awards Dinner in New York City on Thursday.
Love must have been in the air all day because earlier on Friday, the songstress tweeted, 'i cant believe my life rn tbh if i'm dreaming pls knock me the f–k back out.'
Along with celebrating fans are celebrating friends of the couple.
