Whether you treat them to a home-cooked meal with one of the best recipe boxes, an experience on their bucket list or a luxury gift they'll treasure for years to come – Father's Day is a great time to show the father figures in your life how much you appreciate them.
Father's Day lands on Sunday 16 June in the UK this year, and if you're still struggling for gift ideas look no further. Our edit of the best Father's Day gifts includes tokens of appreciation for fitness loving dads, foodie dads and dads who value their self-care time.
We've also got wellness experiences, must-have fashion for the summer season and investment watches and sunglasses for an extra-special gift. And, if you can't see your dad this year, we've included luxury hampers and letterbox gift ideas so you can still treat them from afar.
See Red's edit of the best Father's Day gifts for 2024 below...
A luxury bathrobe is always a great gift. The White Company's unisex robe is made from cosy, moisture-wicking and fast drying cotton.
The Always Pan from Our Place is the perfect present for foodie dads who love a new kitchen gadget. The do-it-all pan is a bestseller for a reason – it can do eight jobs in one. Impressive.
For the gym-goer, a sweat bag is an essential for keeping sweaty workout kit separate from the rest of their bag. La Pochette's antibacterial and water-resistant pouch stops bacteria and odour in its tracks. Made from 100% recycled plastic bottles, it's a sustainable alternative to plastic bags.
You can't go wrong with a cotton pyjama set. The subtle polka dot print adds a touch of luxury to this traditional button-through style from M&S .
Celebrate Father's Day with a bottle of this divine Champagne , a treat for your dad and for you!
A pair of new sunglasses will be a welcome treat given the time of year. Ace & Tate's rounded Benjamin shades come in a choice of six frames with anti-scratch lens coating.
A breathable linen-blend shirt in a khaki and white stripe will make a classic addition to his holiday wardrobe.
Aptly names the True Gentleman’s Hamper, this luxury collection of goodies has all your dad needs for a delicious treat on his special day. There’s everything from a bottle of red wine and decadent chocolate truffles to stuffed olives and aromatic ground coffee inside this wicker basket.
A treat for the book loving dad – this gift package includes a top-rated book, plus six craft beers from a mix of breweries.
Hello Fresh customers will be able to add this Father's Day steak menu to their order this June. Priced at £4.99 per person, it includes a Garlic & Chive Butter 21 Day Aged Sirloin Steak served alongside Cheesy Bacon Hasselback Potatoes and Baby Leaf Salad.
Is he in need of a watch upgrade? We love Sekonda's classic leather strap watch with a gold case and white face – it'll last him years to come.
Can't see your dad for Father's Day this year? Have chocolate brownies delivered straight to his door, thanks to trusty M&S.
If a luxury gift is on the cards, the cult Hydrow Rower will go down well with fitness-loving dads – helping them stay fit from the comfort of their own home.
