Shannon Beador was exposed as hiding a boyfriend during the last season of The Real Housewives of Orange County
The 13th season of the Bravo show had focused heavily on Shannon's painful split from her husband of 20 years, David, with her now admitting he lives with a new woman rumored to be pregnant.
Shannon, 54, was confronted on the second part of the reunion special about her secret love life with even host Andy Cohen, 50, clearly shocked by the news.
Secret boyfriend: Shannon Beador was exposed as hiding a secret boyfriend on Sunday's second part of The Real Housewives Of Orange Country Reunion on Bravo
Tamra Judge , 51, spilled the beans after the former friends once again went after each other, with Tamra screaming: 'This is why I can't tell you anything! You always turn it on me!'
She then left Shannon clearly shocked as she said: 'I get frustrated because she sits there and she's like, ''No, I'm not dating. I'm not dating.''
'You were dating a guy when we were filming!,' Tamra declared.
'Oh, so you had a boyfriend the whole season?' Andy quickly asked.
While filming: Tamra Judge revealed that Shannon was dating a guy while filming season 13 of RHOC
'I liked him, I really liked him, but he was a jerk to me,' Shannon insisted, making it clear they were no longer together.
Gina Kirschenheiter, 34, expressed her resentment that Shannon would allow her to miss time with her kids to instead find her a matchmaker.
'I was sitting on the phone with the matchmaker caring about you, excited about getting you this date, and then I find out you had a boyfriend the whole time,' Gina complained.
Together again: Gina KIrschenhelter, Kelly Dodd, Tamra, Andy Cohen, Shannon, Vicki Gunvalson and Emily Simpson gathered for the season 13 reunion
Tamra continued: 'You play victim a lot. You're like, ''David was dating three months after. He's dating. It's hard for me ... '' You were too! You were dating, too!
'Your two favorite words are me and I. Me, me, me, I, I, I, poor, poor, poor, victim, victim, victim. And sometimes, it gets wearing on me,' Tamra admitted.
Shannon replied: 'To hear that it was so exhausting and horrible for you to be there for me ... That's the definition of a good friendship.
'He cheated on me and I went through that in the public eye.'
Public eye: Shannon reminded everyone that her ex-husband David cheated on her and she went through a public divorce
Tamra snapped: 'I know, it's been four years, five years.'
The revelation came after Shannon had already been asked about her dating life.
'I'm out, and that's what I want,' she said happily.
'If I meet the right person that's what I want and that'd be great. But for now it's fun to get excited about meeting people and doing different things.
Good times: The reunion brought a smile to Shannon, Vicki and Emily
'David wasn't the most social person so I didn't really go out much.'
Andy then left an awkward silence after he said: 'Well, David didn't have a problem meeting other people while you were together ...'
Shannon earlier spoke of her divorce from David, admitting that it was not finalized and was getting even uglier with potential custody issues over their daughters Stella, Sophie and Adeline.
She admitted that David was living with a new partner, someone she did not know but that the girls 'like her.'
Bravo show: The women continued to air out their differences during the reunion
'My thing all along is if someone is good to my kids then I'm good with it,' she said.
When Andy asked if it was true the new lover was pregnant, Shannon pulled a face as she said, 'There's a rumor out there.'
She then got emotional saying she was 'walking on eggshells,' explaining: 'I want their dad to be a part of their life. But because now custody might be an issue, I'm supposed to give my children their space.'
The host: Andy Cohen, center, moderated the reunion
She was also sarcastic with Andy for screening her drunken moments in Mexico, saying: 'Thank you, thank you for showing that.'
She then insisted that her ex had used it as part of their legal fight, saying: 'When you're going through an acrimonious divorce and potential custody issues you bring up behavior of your ex-spouse that is maybe not appropriate.
Emily, a lawyer, said: 'Her behavior while on a girls' trip isn't relevant to how she treats her children or what kind of mom she is.
'You can go on a trip with your girlfriends and drink and have fun without your children being there. That's not a detriment to your children in any way, shape or form.'
United front: The women presented a united front as they got together at the reunion
Shannon also defended paying so much attention to her weight issues, saying: 'There's not a person that beats themselves up more than me. I've been a small girl my whole life and I just want to get back there. And I'm very proud of myself that I am getting there.
'Where I am right now I am very excited for the future,' Shannon said.
Show newcomer Emily Simpson, however, got tearful as she admitted getting spiteful body shaming messages on social media.
'That was hard,' she said, wiping away tears. 'I never looked at myself as fat.
'I knew I was bigger -- I mean, I'm a large female -- but I've never looked at myself and been, ''Oh you're disgusting.''
Finger point: Emily pointed a finger as she spoke
'It was women ... they would send me direct messages on Instagram and call me a fat ass, disgusting, I needed to lose weight, I'm not healthy, how could I go out like that ... I mean it was horrible.
'It made me want to fight back but in a positive way. I'm gonna use it as a positive and say, ''You know what, I like the way I look. I'm confident.'' We don't have to the same size to feel beautiful or sexy. All women deserve to feel like that.'
Shannon told her: 'People are nasty when they can hide behind the keyboards.'
Vicki Gunvalson, meanwhile, apologized to Kelly for claiming she used cocaine, which outraged Kelly as a mother.
'I don't blame her for being hurt, and I'm sorry,' Vicki, 56, told her. 'That was a rumor that came around, and I'm sorry for repeating a rumor.'
