When we really like something, you can trust that our opinion has come from vetting it against everything we've seen before, including our longtime favorites. (We've even written love letters to some of the products we hold most dear.) But we're always open to finding — and sharing — new favorites. It's a big beauty playground out there, so we'll gladly do the dirty work to test everything under the sun. And the crème de la crème often graduate to our Best of Beauty trials.
But let's stick to the present for now. Each week, Allure editors select the new hair, makeup, and skin-care products we're currently obsessing over. Trying to narrow down our favorites to just one or two products can be hard, but we manage. Check out what our editors can't get enough of right now.
In the midst of taking a month off from heat styling, I found myself searching for an edge tamer to achieve my go-to slicked-back hairstyles throughout the work week. This bouncy Mizani Artful Edges Edge Tamer did exactly that, controlling my stubborn grays and flyaways — without flaking throughout the day. Made with shea butter and castor oil, my edges and defined middle part stayed sleek, not crunchy. The sweet but subtle fruity scent doesn't hurt either. — Talia Gutierrez, associate special projects manager
We've seen an abundance of great blush launches already this year, but so far Half Magic Cheek Fluff is my favorite. It has such a unique texture that feels like putty in the palette but blends into your skin with a powdery finish. I opt for a brush to apply and have been alternating between (Don't) Be a Doll (a peachy bubblegum) and Magic Brownie (a warm brown) — they're both just neutral enough to go with any makeup look I'm trying. — Kara McGrath, deputy digital director
Hope Night Body Butter is a body cream that can double as my fragrance. I slather it on from my chest down to my feet and the combination of coconut oil and shea butter makes my skin feel super soft. What I love most though is the delicious aroma — a rich vanilla that's been livened up with hints of amber and patchouli — it leaves behind. — Gabi Thorne, associate news editor
Since its recent launch, Tom Ford Electric Cherry Eau de Parfum has already become a mainstay in my spring fragrance wardrobe, especially when I want to smell sexy. Ultra-sweet cherries are mixed with spicy ginger and warm musk, for a scent that is reminiscent of a body mist from my teens… though it's much more elevated. — Jennifer Hussein, commerce writer
Usually, I find moisturizers underwhelming, but the Iope Stem III Cream caught my attention. I was impressed by its cool, gel-cream texture (infused with smoothing niacinamide and hydrating glycerin) and how easily it sinks into my skin. I use it both morning and night: it's light enough to wear under my sunscreen during the day and provides heavy-duty hydration before bed. — Annie Blay, associate beauty editor
At this point, my bikini line and ingrown hairs basically have a common-law marriage — at times it seems impossible to separate them. That's why products like Billie Ultimate Skin Solution are such lifesavers. This spray-on liquid contains salicylic acid which, as you know, chemically unclogs pores, while its aloe soothes skin that's been through the wringer when it comes to shaving and waxing. With just a few spritzes down there every couple of days, I've been able to address a near-life-long skin issue. — Nicola Dall’Asen, news editor
Fenty Beauty Icon Semi Matte Refillable Lipsticks were designed to have the same shape as Rihanna's Cupid's bow — and the design plus the creamy texture (with moisturizing hyaluronic acid and soothing vitamin E) allow them to swipe on perfectly. Unlike traditional matte lipstick that can be drying, these bullets won't cause lips to flake or crack. The color is buttery-smooth and opaque, with a true semi-matte finish (it’s got just a teensy bit of shine, which looks fresh on your lips). When I wore The MVP [a vibrant red shade], hours went by and the color was just as striking as when I applied it — without any feathering or fading. — Paige Stables, senior beauty editor
We love it so much that for a limited time we're giving it to new members as a free welcome gift with the April 2023 Allure Beauty Box. You can score the Allure Beauty Box here for access to even more editor favorites — starting at just $25.
I've put a self-imposed moratorium on hair gel for the better part of a decade. (If you have ultra-fine strands, like I do, perhaps you can relate.) Turns out, technology has come a long way in ten years — and Odele Flex Hair Gel is case in point. Unlike the goopy, greasy formulas I'd used in the past, this one is incredibly lightweight and blissfully free of crunch, providing just the right amount of hold to tame errant flyaways. — Dianna Mazzone, associate features director
I was hesitant about trying Ellis Brooklyn Satisfying Skin Caring Moisturizer in the winter since it's a super light, cloud-like texture that I assumed would be better suited for hotter and more humid weather. I'm thrilled I didn't wait! Even though the cream feels almost weightless, it gave my skin plenty of hydration (thanks to squalene and niacinamide ) while creating a slight blurring effect that made the moisturizer a great base for wearing under makeup. — Kara McGrath, deputy digital director
I'm a big fan of floral fragrances, so when Aerin Rose De Grasse Joyful Bloom launched, I had a feeling I would love it. And as soon as I spritzed it on, this was 100% confirmed. Roses (Indian Rose Bourboniana and Turkish Rose, to be exact) smell brand new in this blend of Italian bergamot, pink pepper, and Australian sandalwood. It's like a classic bouquet with a twist. — Gabi Thorne, associate news editor
When you've dyed your hair a vivid color — like bright orange — as I have, you avoid washing your hair in order to maintain said color. Currently, dry shampoo is the only thing staving off my oil-prone roots and protecting my hair dye from the clarifying clutches of most shampoos. Olaplex No.4D Clean Volume Detox Dry Shampoo might be the best one I've come across. About once a week, I section out my hair and spray on the dry shampoo, focusing mostly on my center part and around the crown of my hair — that's where I'm the oiliest. And I'm happy to say, this formula doesn't leave behind that dreaded stiff feeling and white cast. — Nicola Dall’Asen, news editor
I cannot get over how glowy the Kevyn Aucoin Stripped Nude Skin Tint makes my face look. I prefer to mix two shades (Light 01 and Light 02), which I combine on the back of my hand before applying with a dense foundation brush. To make sure it's blended out, I go over my face with a fluffy foundation brush. The finish is quite dewy, but that doesn't seem to impede its lasting power; it doesn't get patchy or oily, even when in warm or humid conditions. — Sam Escobar, site director
I have dark circles, and while concealer does an okay job covering them up, after a few hours, grey undertones start to peek through. But since discovering the Make Up For Ever Color Correcting Step 1 Primers: Grayness Reducer , this is no longer a concern. The formula feels hydrating like a normal primer but also deposits an orange pigment that cancels out any greyness or dark spots on my face. It makes my undereye makeup look seamless — and it doesn’t feel like I’m adding a whole extra step to my routine. — Annie Blay, associate beauty editor
