708371865600	858534830266433536	858539335909617664	858546056199630848	858652344703225856	858652571384336385	858653792849596416	858655724930568196	858684289709420544	858706611858268160	858722277982130176	858723003621941249	858781950827429890	858913671459643392	859054804751888384	859125271122788352	859128900215033857	859130950390820868	859132862595035136	859987396682764289	859994345344307200	860340953969807360	860498913337503744	863486771467763712	863487018411581441	865736027725496320	865738359959715840	868502615394590722	872816030585954305	872909021325533185	873111309880926208,0,variety.com,44,"Harry Styles took to Twitter Friday morning to announce the dates for his first solo world tour, Harry Styles Live On Tour. It will begin Sept. 19 in the United States and end in Japan in early December.
All tickets go on sale on Friday, May 5 (excluding Japan) via local ticketing agents. Those sales begin just a week ahead of the debut of Styles’ self-titled debut album, which will be released May 12.
Fan registration for all North American dates has commenced, though supplies are limited.  To prevent other vendors from re-selling tickets at higher prices, concert-goers can sign up for Ticketmaster’s Verified Fan program.
