gossipcop-842417,https://www.bustle.com/p/why-are-thor-the-hulk-fighting-in-the-thor-ragnarok-trailer-the-first-look-is-so-exciting-50110,Why Are Thor & The Hulk Fighting In the 'Thor: Ragnarok' Trailer? The First Look Is So Exciting,851428685324406784	851428866304462849	851428899162640384	851429366294863872	851429471232118784	851429537816752128	851429579898068995	851429582985019393	851429625615929344	851429735775313921	851429902746341376	851429926066630658	851430382314573824	851430667728695296	851430967449407489	851431057622695936	851431121854369792	851431283951493120	851431596393672704	851431828288192513	851432136028467201	851432174515388417	851432202722091008	851432354383974405	851432370720784384	851432375225532416	851432374894157825	851432377616187393	851432380774588416	851432386566905856	851432391793033218	851432510302978048	851432531958390784	851432596730814464	851432647825817605	851433134348546048	851433494148374529	851434110945853440	851434896304226305	851434901555470339	851434906886393857	851434913341480961	851434912741642240	851434925928480768	851434924447903744	851435120053669888	851436116674609156	851440829512249344	851441415351668737	851444574295805952	851444589160415233	851444593631518721	851444592121487361	851444598194880513	851444596168990720	851444595506294784	851449093020954624	851449860440039424	851449864546164736	851449965381427202	851451009209688064	851451229842554880	851454919777415168	851459076101820416	851459090807111680	851470538715258880	851482721708720128	851483697488338944	851488008582815744	851572498894389249	851623392243585024	852159480397787136,0,bustle.com,95,"Have you ever had an unexpected run in with an old co-worker? In the latest trailer for Marvel's Thor: Ragnarok, Thor finds himself fighting the Hulk in a massive battle arena. The gladiator-esque face off is not exactly a warm reunion between two former Avengers, and it creates a lot of questions. At first Thor seems relieved to run into a familiar face, even if that face is enormous, angry, and green. For a small moment it appears the superhero might be in the clear, but that would be too simple, and the Hulk doesn't seem to recognize his old pal. Instead, the Hulk charges full throttle toward Thor, and right before the two meet in the air the trailer cuts to black.
So, what's going on here? It's clear that something fishy is afoot, or the Hulk wouldn't be trying to clobber a superhero he used to fight evil with. It might have a lot to do with the Grandmaster, a decadently dressed yet rather sinister new villain played by Jeff Goldblum . The Grandmaster seems to be orchestrating this whole fight, and can be seen looking on in disapproval from a skybox above the arena. The big mystery is how the character got the Hulk to turn on a friend. ""Oh, come on,"" Thor says in frustration as the Hulk growls at his friendly approach, and as viewers, we can relate.
Of course, the face off between Thor and the Hulk isn't the only excitement in the new trailer. This is the big reveal of Cate Blanchett's Hela, the Asgardian goddess of death, a character expected to challenge the series' protagonist in a major way. ""She plays the worst of the worst. So evil,"" Mark Ruffalo, who plays the Hulk, described Blanchett's character in an interview with ET Online . ""She is going to kill us. It's such a great part she gets to play.""
Even without Blanchett's Oscar-winning acting, the film is packed with stars. Tom Hiddleston reprises his role as Loki, who can only be back once more to try and defeat Thor. It also appears Benedict Cumberbatch will make a high-profile appearance as Doctor Strange, and Tessa Thompson ( Creed , Westworld ) will play the Asgardian superhero Valkyrie. Anthony Hopkins will once again appear as Odin, and Idris Elba returns as Heimdall. On the performance front, this is not the Marvel movie to miss.
Let's just hope that the Hulk recognizes Thor at some point, because it looks like the hero might be in a bit of trouble. It's going to take a lot to defeat Blanchett's Hela, who was a scary enough villain before they introduced that hat with the evil mutant deer horns and thorn studded sword in this trailer. That's not to mention the evil work of Loki and the Grandmaster, who are just two more obstacles in the way of saving Asgard.
The film hits theaters on November 3, 2017, and director Taika Waititi has promised in interviews that even for a superhero movie, it will be truly strange and ""out there"". This first look trailer definitely supports that claim, but let's just hope we get a few more answers before the movie premieres in the fall.",ok
gossipcop-923731,https://www.etonline.com/jeff-goldblum-reveals-his-moms-terrified-reaction-to-his-infamous-death-hoax-99308,Jeff Goldblum Reveals His Mom's Terrified Reaction to His Infamous Death Hoax,979088360634380288	979088489441628160	979088679619751936	979089644154441729	979089853047558144	979090111009906688	979090225296179207	979090712208789504	979091001900900352	979091088051986432	979093528021295105	979093537433276422	979096146466390016	979099086682054656	979102739044225025	979104815954280449	979111197503995904	979116279721111552	979123836607016960	979129145673199616	979136267454590977	979143668962533376	979146648038277120	979148589577351168	979153940737548288	979160998178275329	979166595422470144	979173908627664897	979179412112359426	979186490876993536	979192015509364736	979198762634506240	979200718623125505	979204514266824704	979211518616117248	979214463340511236	979214496907526145	979214519984705541	979217160613457920	979224635731423233	979232186082648064	979241995582361601	979249461187592192	979253456098811905	979255193572429827	979256630020747264	979261214239969280	979261732156710912	979267117575946240	979274891827412992	979274906373316609	979284493948211200	979290191079682049	979297306238320645	979304921873899520	979314367702253568	979320006872674305	979325234812674048	979523175657611264	981205165221888000,0,etonline.com,77,"Celebrity death hoaxes have become an internet staple, and one of the most frequent targets is beloved eccentric Jeff Goldblum.
The Jurassic Park star first became the victim of a fake obit in 2009 when rumors began circulating on Facebook that he died after falling off a cliff in New Zealand while filming a new project.
First created by internet trolls and social media opportunists, and then spread by legitimately bereaved friends and unreputable blogs, the story took off like wildfire. And while Goldblum knew first-hand that he was still alive, many of his friends and family didn't have that luxury.
Speaking with The Talk on Wednesday, the 65-year-old actor -- who is currently starring in Wes Anderson's animated dramedy Isle of Dogs -- reflected on how the hoax really scared his mother.
""It went all over the world for a little bit for a couple of hours before I could set the record straight,"" Goldblum recalled. ""So people thought that I'd died. And those were the days when I had a telephone landline and my answering machine and before I could call everybody, I got a couple of messages that I wasn't able to pick up, from like, my mother. It was, 'Jeffrey, are you there? Are you there?'""
""So be careful about gossip,"" he added. ""Be careful about spreading something that you haven't sourced entirely or that's not factual.""
On Monday, Goldblum sat down on Watch What Happens Live with Andy Cohen where he also reflected on the death hoax -- which has resurfaced several times in the years since it first went viral -- and said that he got another message at the time from a close friend who ""very tearfully and hysterically left a message"" trying to find out if he was actually dead.
In reality, Goldblum told the New Zealand Herald in 2016 that not only has he never shot a film in the country, he's never even been there at all. And now, in the light of the hoax, he's not sure if he ever should visit.
""Could you imagine if that's the way I go?"" Goldblum joked. ""Wow. Could you imagine? 'They foretold the future, he actually did fall off a cliff in New Zealand.' It's got to happen some way!""
In real life, Goldblum is actually healthy and happy and will soon be seen on the big screen reprising his role as mathematician and dino-adventurer Dr. Ian Malcolm in the upcoming Jurassic World: Forbidden Kingdom.
Recently, the star sat down with ET where he opened up about returning to the mega-popular franchise and the possibility of his former co-star, Laura Dern , coming back to reprise her role as paleobotanist Ellie Sattler.
""I don't want to pass on gossip like my character,"" Goldblum said, ""but it would be good news to me and to everyone, [to] millions and billions of people all over the world… all over the universe and cosmos when Ellie Sattler returns.""
Check out the video below to hear more from Goldblum about Fallen Kingdom , which stampedes into theaters June 22.",ok
